# Retirement of the legacy niobespagiftcard.com application.
#
# This file ADDS a gate. It renames nothing and deletes nothing, so the whole
# change is undone by deleting this one file — which is the only reason it is
# safe to apply to a live site before the database has been dumped.
#
# What it shuts, and why:
#   api/       — api/callback.php sets its "was this paid?" flag from the JSON
#                posted to it. No signature, no shared secret, no IP allow-list,
#                and the posted Amount is never compared to the order total, so
#                any stranger who posts a pending reference is issued a funded
#                voucher. This is the reason the gate exists at all.
#   backoffice/— admin login whose seed password is named, in plain sight, by a
#                leftover backoffice/hash.php that prints password_hash() of a
#                hardcoded throwaway. The page guards are sound; the credential is
#                the problem, and a login nobody uses is a login nobody is watching.
#   cron/      — reachable over HTTP as well as by the scheduler. Both scripts
#                send customer email AND write to the database (auto-cancel,
#                expire). Nothing that mutates rows should be triggerable by URL.
#
# Everything else lands on holding.html. Deliberately 410 Gone rather than 404
# for the retired endpoints: it is accurate, and it tells any caller still
# pointed here (Hubtel included) to stop, instead of implying a typo.

Options -Indexes
DirectoryIndex holding.html

<IfModule mod_rewrite.c>
  RewriteEngine On

  # Retired application surfaces — refuse outright, before anything executes.
  RewriteRule ^(api|backoffice|cron)(/|$) - [G,L]

  # Serve the holding page itself and its assets normally.
  RewriteRule ^holding\.html$ - [L]
  RewriteRule ^assets/images/logo/ - [L]

  # Everything else: the holding page, at the URL the visitor asked for.
  RewriteRule ^ /holding.html [L]
</IfModule>

# Belt and braces for hosts where mod_rewrite is unavailable: still no PHP.
<FilesMatch "\.(php|phtml|phar)$">
  Require all denied
</FilesMatch>
